    {
      "sectionId": "section-disclaimer",
      "heading": "Understanding RPGBOT’s Rating System",
      "sourceAnchor": "disclaimer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "RPGBOT uses a color coding scheme which is simple to understand and easy to read at a glance. This system is designed to help players make informed decisions for their dnd character builds."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-2",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Red"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Bad, useless options, or options which\n\t\tare extremely situational. Nearly never useful."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Orange"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": OK options, or useful options\n\t\tthat only apply in rare circumstances. Useful sometimes."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Green"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Good options. Useful often."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Blue"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Fantastic options, often essential\n\t\tto the function of your character. Useful very frequently."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "depths": [
            0,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "itemKinds": [
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered"
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The advice in this article is based on the current "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "State of the 2024 DnD Character Optimization Meta",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/2024-dnd-meta/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " as of when the article was last updated. Keep in mind that the state of the meta periodically changes as new source materials are released, and the article will be updated accordingly as time allows. Also be sure to check for "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "errata",
              "href": "https://www.dndbeyond.com/changelog#2024CoreRulesErrata"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " periodically."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "We will not include 3rd-party content, Unearthed Arcnaa content, or homebrew in guides for official content because we can’t assume that your game will allow them."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-changes-from-the-2014-dnd-5e-rules-to-the-2024-dnd-55-rules",
      "heading": "Changes from the 2014 DnD 5e Rules to the 2024 DnD 5.5 Rules",
      "sourceAnchor": "changes-from-the-2014-dnd-5e-rules-to-the-2024-dnd-55-rules",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-changes-from-the-2014-dnd-5e-rules-to-the-2024-dnd-55-rules-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A few changes were made between editions:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-changes-from-the-2014-dnd-5e-rules-to-the-2024-dnd-55-rules-2",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Ancestral Legacy was removed"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Deathless Nature was removed"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Trace of Undeath (resistance to Necrotic damage) was added"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Vampiric Bite is no longer a simple weapon and is instead an unarmed strike, it no longer provides Advantage on attacks while you’re below half hit points, and the attack/check bonus now expires after 1 minute"
              }
            ]
          ],
          "depths": [
            0,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "itemKinds": [
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-dhampir-traits",
      "heading": "Dhampir Traits",
      "sourceAnchor": "dhampir-traits",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-dhampir-traits-1",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "type": "strong",
                "text": "Size"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Your choice of small or medium. There are nearly no\n\t\tmeaningful distinctions between Small and Medium size. Small characters can\n\t\tbe swallowed whole more easily and have lower carrying capacity, but can\n\t\tride smaller mounts."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Speed"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Slightly better than normal."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Darkvision"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Essential."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Spider Climb"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": The next best thing to\n\t\tflying."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Trace of Undeath"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Only situationall\n\t\tuseful, but I’ll never complain about a permanent damage resistance."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Vampiric Bite"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": See below."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "depths": [
            0,
            0,
            0,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "itemKinds": [
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-vampiric-bite",
      "parentSectionId": "section-dhampir-traits",
      "heading": "Vampiric Bite",
      "sourceAnchor": "vampiric-bite",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-vampiric-bite-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Vampiric Bite is an unarmed strike and follows most of the normal rules for\n\tunarmed strikes, but applies your Constitution modifier to damage instead of\n\tStrength. The damage won’t be fantastic, but the primary function of the bite\n\tis to apply one of the two rider effects."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-vampiric-bite-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Drain lets you heal yourself. The more damage you do, the more healing you\n\tcan get. The normal damage of 1d4 + Con won’t have a big impact beyond low\n\tlevels, unfortunately, unless you find ways to improve your damage."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-vampiric-bite-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Strengthen lets you give yourself a bonus to your next attack or ability\n\tcheck within the next minute. 1d4 + Con is already a really nice bonus, but\n\twith a critical hit and sources of additional damage, you could get the bonus\n\thigh enough that you can’t fail the roll. If you’re outside of combat and want\n\tthe bonus on checks, pretend you’re Astarion and eat a rat."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-vampiric-bite-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Piercer feat is very useful here, as it provides both a die reroll and\n\tadditional damage die on crit. If you can guarantee a critical hit somehow,\n\tthis can make Vampiric Bite’s effects considerably more useful. Magic items\n\tlike Wraps of Unarmed Power are similarly useful."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-vampiric-bite-5",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Vampiric Bite’s rider effects only care about the piercing damage dealt by\n\tthe attack. Common damage boosts like Divine Smite (Radiant), Hex (Necrotic),\n\tand Hunter’s Mark (Force) won’t help here."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-vampiric-bite-6",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "It’s not totally clear how Vampiric Bite interacts with other mechanics that\n\tchange your unarmed strike damage, such as Monk levels. I think the intent is\n\tthat you can only use Drain and Strengthen if you stick to the 1d4 + Con bite\n\tdamage, but your DM might allow you to use your Martial Arts damage die."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-vampiric-bite-7",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "While changing the damage of Vampiric Bite is unclear, changing the attack\n\tappears to work like any other unarmed strike. The wording of Vampiric Bite\n\tallows to choose to bite “when you hit and deal damage”, so it has no\n\tinteraction with the attack roll mechanic. This means that you’re free to take\n\ta level of Monk to change your Unarmed Strikes to use Dexterity instead of\n\tStrength."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Dhampir Classes",
      "sourceAnchor": "classes",
      "blocks": []
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-artificer",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Artificer",
      "sourceAnchor": "artificer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-artificer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Artificer makes a lot of the Dhampir’s traits redundant. You can use\n\tInfusions to deal with breathing, to see in the dark, to walk on walls (or\n\tfly, preferably), to heal, and to buff your skill checks (Enhance Ability).\n\tThe Dhampir may enable you to skip over some options for Infusions and spells,\n\tbut the Artificer’s class features can often handle those challenges better,\n\tso your racial traits may feel redundant and will gradually become obsolete as\n\tyou gain levels."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-barbarian",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Barbarian",
      "sourceAnchor": "barbarian",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-barbarian-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Vampiric Bite is a great complement to the Barbarian’s abilities, offering a\n\tway to heal yourself in combat and to boost your attacks and checks to\n\tovercome significant challenges. With Reckless Attack you’ll be able to hit\n\twith Vampiric Bite reliably when you need to use it in combat."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-barbarian-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Beyond that, the Dhampir provides a lot of things that Barbarians can’t\n\treplicate. Darkvision, Spider Climb to get over obstacles, and a damage\n\tresistance."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-barbarian-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "At high levels, the Barbarian’s Brutal Strike can add additional damage to\n\tVampiric Bite, allowing you to heal more or get a bigger attack/check bonus.\n\tPiercer is also an easy choice for the Barbarian, offering additional damage\n\twith weapons like tridents and pikes."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-bard",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Bard",
      "sourceAnchor": "bard",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-bard-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "For caster Bards, the ability to walk on walls and ceilings is a great way to\n\tstay out of reach of enemies without spending expensive spell slots on flight.\n\tVampiric Bite won’t be useful in combat, but it’s great for the boost to\n\tability checks."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-cleric",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Cleric",
      "sourceAnchor": "cleric",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-cleric-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "For caster Clerics, the ability to walk on walls and ceilings is a great way\n\tto stay out of reach of enemies. Vampiric Bite won’t be useful in combat, but\n\tit’s great for the boost to ability checks."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-druid",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Druid",
      "sourceAnchor": "druid",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-druid-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "None of the things that make the Dhampir interesting function in Wild Shape,\n\tand the Druid can replicate most of the Dhampir’s exciting features with some\n\tcombination of spells and Wild Shape."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-fighter",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Fighter",
      "sourceAnchor": "fighter",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-fighter-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A Strength-based Fighter is perfectly equipped to make Unarmed Strikes, which\n\tis all that you need to benefit from Vampiric Bite. Darkvision is great,\n\tSpider Climb provides mobility that most Fighters can’t replicate, and you get\n\ta damage resistance."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-fighter-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "If you want to fight at range, the ability to walk on walls/ceilings without\n\tthe aid of spells or magic items is a great asset, and you can relegate\n\tVampiric Bite to empowering ability checks outside of combat."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-monk",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Monk",
      "sourceAnchor": "monk",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-monk-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Relying on unarmed strikes makes it very easy to slip Vampiric Bite into a\n\tturn. Spider Climb works with the Monk’s crazy speed. Darkvision and a damage\n\tresistance are always nice."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-monk-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Because of the way Vampiric Bite is worded, you make the attack roll before\n\tyou decide to bite, which means that you can definitely use Martial Arts to\n\tattack with Dexterity. However, it’s not totally clear if your Martial Arts\n\tdie can replace the 1d4 damage die on Vampiric Bite. Generally, when you have\n\tmultiple options to change a value, you get to choose which to use (ex:\n\tUnarmored Defense), but the wording on Vampiric Bite sounds like you need to\n\tdecide to use 1d4 + Con to use the rest of the feature. Talk to your DM."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-monk-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "If your DM allows you to use your Martial Arts die for Vampiric Bite, the\n\tMonk is "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "blue."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-paladin",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Paladin",
      "sourceAnchor": "paladin",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-paladin-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A Strength-based Paladin is perfectly equipped to make Unarmed Strikes, which\n\tis all that you need to benefit from Vampiric Bite. Darkvision is great,\n\tSpider Climb provides mobility that most Paladins can’t replicate until your\n\tsteed can fly, and you get a damage resistance."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-ranger",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Ranger",
      "sourceAnchor": "ranger",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-ranger-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Strength-based Rangers are weak, so Vampiric Bite isn’t useful in combat\n\tunless you multiclass into Monk. Darkvision, Spider Climb, and a damage\n\tresistance."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-ranger-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "If you want to fight at range, the ability to walk on walls/ceilings without\n\tthe aid of spells or magic items is a great asset, and you can relegate\n\tVampiric Bite to empowering ability checks outside of combat."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-rogue",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Rogue",
      "sourceAnchor": "rogue",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-rogue-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Vampiric Bite doesn’t qualify for Sneak Attack, which is disappointing\n\tbecause I’m sure there are legions of players hoping to play an edgy dhampir\n\trogue. Darkvision and the ability to climb walls and ceilings solves a lot of\n\tproblems which often require magic, and Vampiric Bite can still be used to\n\tempower attacks and ability checks, so there is still some value here, though\n\tyou almost certainly won’t use Vampiric Bite in combat."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-sorcerer",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Sorcerer",
      "sourceAnchor": "sorcerer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-sorcerer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The ability to walk on walls/ceilings makes flight less crucial, but at that\n\tpoint, a race with flight is significantly more effective, or you can cast\n\tSpider Climb. Vampiric Bite may be helpful for ability checks outside of\n\tcombat, but eating rats in the middle of social situations may be frowned\n\tupon."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-warlock",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Warlock",
      "sourceAnchor": "warlock",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-warlock-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The ability to walk on walls/ceilings makes flight less crucial, but at that\n\tpoint, a race with flight is significantly more effective, or you can cast\n\tSpider Climb. Vampiric Bite may be helpful for ability checks outside of\n\tcombat, but eating rats in the middle of social situations may be frowned\n\tupon."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-wizard",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes",
      "heading": "Wizard",
      "sourceAnchor": "wizard",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-wizard-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The ability to walk on walls/ceilings makes flight less crucial, but at that\n\tpoint, a race with flight is significantly more effective, or you can cast\n\tSpider Climb. Vampiric Bite may be helpful for ability checks outside of\n\tcombat. Eating a rat for a skill bonus before making knowledge skill checks\n\tcan be very useful."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-wizard-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Unfortunately, Vampiric Bite won’t be useful for Bladesingers since Unarmed\n\tStrikes are Strength-based. You could multiclass into Monk to make them\n\tDexterity-based, but it’s not worth that cost."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
